# coach-sync — SERVER environment file.
#
# Copy to ~/homelab/services/coach-sync/.env ON THE SERVER and fill in.
# That file is untracked, lives only on the box, and must never be committed
# to either repo. This example is committed; it must never contain a value.
#
#   scp deploy/.env.example homelab:/tmp/coach-sync.env.example
#   ssh homelab 'mkdir -p ~/homelab/services/coach-sync && \
#                mv /tmp/coach-sync.env.example ~/homelab/services/coach-sync/.env'
#   ssh -t homelab 'nano ~/homelab/services/coach-sync/.env'   # paste the values
#   ssh homelab 'chmod 600 ~/homelab/services/coach-sync/.env'
#
# ⚠️ Anything pasted into a chat window is compromised. Type these on the box.

# ── Google Health API (OAuth 2.0 refresh-token flow) ───────────────────
# From the Google Cloud OAuth client + the Playground's "Exchange
# authorization code for tokens" step. The container exchanges the refresh
# token for a fresh access token on every run, so no human is in the loop.
#
# ⚠️ The consent screen must be published "In production". While it is in
# "Testing", Google expires refresh tokens after 7 DAYS and the job dies every
# week with `invalid_grant` (ARCHITECTURE.md OQ-5). That failure now alerts on
# Telegram rather than going unnoticed, but it is still a weekly outage.
GHEALTH_CLIENT_ID=
GHEALTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GHEALTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# ── Hevy (requires Hevy Pro) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# https://hevy.com/settings?developer
# ⚠️ This key can WRITE workouts. The pipeline only ever calls read endpoints;
# if that ever changes, review it — a bug that writes to Hevy corrupts the
# lifting record the campaign is scored on.
HEVY_API_KEY=

# ── Telegram alerting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reuse the existing homelab bot (@LEGOBorrowBot) — this service only calls
# sendMessage, so it does NOT conflict with legobot's long-poll (the HTTP 409
# rule applies to getUpdates only). Same TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID as legobot.
#
# Leave these blank and the job still runs — failures just print to the log
# instead of reaching a phone, which is the silent-staleness failure this
# service exists to prevent. Fill them in.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── Optional: a one-off access token, for debugging only ───────────────
# Expires in ~1 hour. Never set this in the container's .env; it exists so a
# human can reproduce a fetch by hand.
# GHEALTH_ACCESS_TOKEN=
